                <pb facs="0430" n="418" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg418"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.20 Mission/7–144: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Ford</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-07-01T18:00:00+03:25">July 1, 1944—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 1—3:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>472. Department’s 243, April 21. Although Legation has approached Foreign
                    Minister several times regarding renewal of agreement on American Military
                    Mission to Iranian <hi rendition="#italic">Gendarmerie</hi> no formal reply has
                    been received. However, Colonel Schwarzkopf today received letter from Minister
                    of Interior stating his desire that agreement be renewed for one additional
                    year. I shall continue to press Saed for formal statement.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ford</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
